Subject: Cantor Composed Read-Only Semantic Inspection P0 Architecture Review

@ [review_uuid] 4edc0c39-e1c1-4d32-9c4b-00a3e0d1ab5f
@ [source_snapshot_uuid] 5ae031ce-6922-4583-85c8-0d3f8e23bd7b
@ [published_predecessor] 06e49668e6881320412151c130518667043fb55d

& [Question]
  + after project assembly semantic find and exact source excerpt are published which next seam most increases usable Cantor behavior without importing host or effect authority

& [Candidates]
  + bounded neighboring source context adds presentation value but does not close caller-side coordination
  + a composed supplied-value inspection request turns the three proven kernels into one auditable semantic transaction
  + filesystem loading or a resident endpoint would increase convenience but crosses an authority boundary not formed in this slice

& [Decision]
  + select the composed supplied-value inspection request
  + bind one supplied project one find request and one fixed exact-source projection under a single request digest
  + return compact assembly coordinates the exact find page and ordered exact excerpts rather than duplicating the complete assembled project in the result
  + preserve existing kernel results as nested evidence and add only cross-result invariants and one outer receipt

& [WhyThisIsHighestLeverage]
  + it creates the first useful read-only inspection transaction that an eventual Eclipse adapter can invoke without reconstructing orchestration semantics
  + it exercises real kernel composition while remaining deterministic provider-free effect-free and independently replayable
  + it exposes whether the existing receipts compose cleanly before any process transport persistence or model surface is authorized

& [FaultBoundary]
  + any assembly query or excerpt refusal aborts the pure computation and produces no partial success result
  + every excerpt must correspond positionally and by record identity to one returned find hit
  + cross-generation assembly-digest query-digest reorder omission duplication and substitution attacks refuse

& [Held]
  + SJS canonicalization requirements matrix phase lock signature Rust implementation instance admission evidence publication and bookend remain future work
  + host loading SQLite persistence cache LSP MCP resident service provider model inference self-update remote execution and all effects remain absent
